{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages.\n\nNow I need to verify the puzzle structure. The Booker Prize was created in 1969, not the 2000s. But the Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (the 2000s). Let me check: \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) was shortlisted for the Booker Prize. In 2019, the Booker Prize was won by \"The Testaments\" by Margaret Atwood (and Bernardine Evaristo's \"Girl, Woman, Other\"). But the puzzle says the award was \"originally created in the 2000s.\"\n\nWait - let me reconsider. The puzzle says the award was created in the 2000s. The Booker Prize (1969) doesn't fit. But the Man Booker International Prize (2005) does. However, Obioma's books were shortlisted for the regular Booker Prize, not the International one.\n\nLet me reconsider whether there's another award. Let me check the 2019 Booker Prize winner and the connection to where Obioma grew up.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma grew up city hometown Nigeria\", \"Booker Prize 2019 winner The Testaments Margaret Atwood\", \"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_e07f535cf8284703aac772ac","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789472919,"id":"chatcmpl-9a7cba4b-0387-9cc3-9b88-b6d8a1c5b351","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":16142,"completion_tokens":319,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":16461,"cached_tokens":11264,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":11264},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}